## 5. Anti-Positioning Generator

At some point, I started explicitly saying who El Mejor was not for.

Not because I wanted to be contrarian. Because it worked.

The moment you say "this isn't for everyone," the people it is for pay attention differently. Exclusion creates belonging. When someone feels like they passed a filter — like the brand actually picked them instead of trying to please a crowd — they hold onto it.

"We're not for people who just want cheap coffee" repelled the price-shoppers. It also told the customer who cares about quality and origin: you're in the right place.

The Anti-Positioning Generator builds your "not for" statements at three levels: soft (clear but gentle), medium (explicit and direct), and sharp (the ones that make some people flinch). It also shows you where to place them — homepage, pricing page, sales conversations, onboarding, email.

You don't have to use the sharpest version. But you should know it exists. The clarity alone sharpens everything else.

