## 6. AI Positioning Sprint

The small agency that repositioned as Agile Marketing Partners didn't spend three months with a consultant.

They ran a 25-minute sprint.

Competitive scan first: how you and your main competitors are currently positioned, what claims are overlapping, where the commoditisation is happening. Then three AI prompts — Blue Ocean Discovery, Weakness-to-Strength, Category Creation — that reveal angles humans miss because they're too close to their own category.

That sprint surfaced the "agility" angle in fifteen minutes. Not because the insight was hidden — it wasn't. It was sitting right there in plain sight. But the agency was too used to apologising for their size to see it as an advantage.

The AI Positioning Sprint is a 25-minute exercise that gives you three credible positioning angles to evaluate. It's not about automating strategy. It's about breaking through the tunnel vision that comes with knowing your business too well.

The agency's closing rate on new business changed significantly after that sprint. The work didn't change. What they said about the work did.

