## 7. Category Creator

At some point, Stupidpreneur stopped competing in the "marketing advice" space and became something different.

Not another marketing newsletter. Not another branding coach. A voice that's honest about what it actually takes to build a brand when you're doing it yourself, without an agency, without a VC, without the luxury of testing everything before it ships.

That's a category. And categories are positions you own rather than fight for.

The Category Creator walks you through five moves: understanding the category you're currently in, identifying the market shift that makes a new one possible, naming the new category, positioning yourself as its creator, and building the "then vs. now" narrative that makes the old approach look outdated.

For Stupidpreneur, the then was "polished marketing advice from people who've never run a bootstrapped business." The now is this — practical, story-based positioning frameworks from someone who's been in the dirt.

When you create a category, competitors aren't competing with you. They're playing a different game. That's the goal.

