## 8. Customer Journey Optimizer

Positioning gets you to the door. The journey gets you through it.

I've seen brands with genuinely strong positioning lose deals they should have won — because the path from "I'm interested" to "I'm buying" had too much friction, too many gaps, too many moments where the customer was left to figure things out alone.

The Customer Journey Optimizer maps where customers drop off and why. Not just the logistics — the emotional experience at each stage. What does someone feel when they first hear about you? What are they unsure about when they're considering? What's the moment they decide to leave instead of convert?

For El Mejor, one of the big drop-off points was first order to second. Customers bought. They loved the coffee. Then nothing brought them back.

The intervention wasn't a discount or a push notification. It was making the second experience feel as personal as the first — a follow-up note, a different farmer's story, a small reason to feel like the relationship had continued. That's emotional journey work, not logistics work.

The six friction dimensions in this tool — cognitive load, trust barriers, information gaps, process complexity, emotional hesitations, competitive alternatives — cover the whole picture. Fix the right one and the rest of your marketing gets dramatically more effective.

